*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─── mobile builds and SIGNING KEYS ────────────────────────────────────────
# The native project itself IS committed, once `npx cap add android` creates it.
# Ignoring the whole android/ tree — which this file used to do — costs more than
# it saves: the app label, the launcher icons and every gradle setting live in
# there, so a fresh clone would rebuild a DIFFERENT app and the published package
# would not be reproducible from this repository. What must never be committed is
# the signing material, and that is named explicitly rather than covered by
# accident. (The same arrangement as a sibling app that has already been
# through a store submission.)
#
# Generated and derived output, rewritten by `cap sync` on every build:
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
android/app/src/main/res/xml/config.xml
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
ios/App/build/
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/App/public/
ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json

# SIGNING MATERIAL — never, under any name. A release key in a public repository
# is unrecoverable: anyone can then publish a package Play accepts as an update
# to this app. These lines exist BEFORE the tree does, so nothing can be staged
# by a careless `git add .`.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
key.properties
keystore.properties
*.aab
*.apk
local.properties
.gradle/
